arkdown":"`review_every_days` (default 7) and `sync_every` (default 6).","startLine":86,"endLine":86,"text":"review_every_days (default 7) and sync_every (default 6)."},{"markdown":"`projects.<p>.kb`: a KB path; see [[cli#Context]].","startLine":87,"endLine":87,"text":"projects.<p>.kb: a KB path; see cli#Context."},{"markdown":"`soul/soul.json` is the SoulSpec v0.5 manifest. `owo stamp` bumps its minor version when a soul file changes.","startLine":89,"endLine":89,"text":"soul/soul.json is the SoulSpec v0.5 manifest. owo stamp bumps its minor version when a soul file changes."},{"markdown":"Each `state.json` has `files`: a map from scope-relative path to `{updated, hash}`. Stamps are RFC 3339 UTC and move only when the hash changes. Hashes are `b3:<blake3 hex>` of the file text.","startLine":93,"endLine":93,"text":"Each state.json has files: a map from scope-relative path to {updated, hash}. Stamps are RFC 3339 UTC and move only when the hash changes. Hashes are b3:<blake3 hex> of the file text."},{"markdown":"`soul/state.json` adds `history` and `review`. Each history record is `{at, file, change, evidence}`, appended by `owo soul note`. The `review` object holds `last_reviewed`, `reviewed_through` and `memory_hash`; when MEMORY.md's hash differs from `memory_hash`, lint warns that MEMORY changed outside a review. `work/state.json` adds `projects`: per project `first_touched`, `last_touched` and `sessions`.","startLine":95,"endLine":95,"text":"soul/state.json adds history and review. Each history record is {at, file, change, evidence}, appended by owo soul note. The review object holds last_reviewed, reviewed_through and memory_hash; when MEMORY.md's hash differs from memory_hash, lint warns that MEMORY changed outside a review. work/state.json adds projects: per project first_touched, last_touched and sessions."},{"markdown":"Commands write JSON files through a temporary file and a rename. A command that rewrites a state file or `soul/soul.json` exits 1 when the file exists but does not parse or is not an object, so a broken file is never replaced with an empty one.","startLine":97,"endLine":97,"text":"Commands write JSON files through a temporary file and a rename. A command that rewrites a state file or soul/soul.json exits 1 when the file exists but does not parse or is not an object, so a broken file is never replaced with an empty one."},{"markdown":"Generated files start with a marker comment and depend only on entry content, so regeneration is deterministic and comparable. Only `owo index` writes them.","startLine":101,"endLine":101,"text":"Generated files start with a marker comment and depend only on entry content, so regeneration is deterministic and comparable. Only owo index writes them."},{"markdown":"Each life category `_index.md` lists `- [[Title]] (marks): summary (aliases: ...)`, where the marks name a `state` other than open (closed, resolved) and a `status` other than canon; location details nest under their overview. `life/_index.md` lists categories with counts. `life/timeline.md` groups events under eras sorted by `date`; `era` resolves like any link (title, alias, slug, `|label`). `work/_index.md` lists the profile and projects with note counts.","startLine":103,"endLine":103,"text":"Each life category _index.md lists - [[Title]] (marks): summary (aliases: ...), where the marks name a state other than open (closed, resolved) and a status other than canon; location details nest under their overview. life/_index.md lists categories with counts. life/timeline.md groups events under eras sorted by date; era resolves like any link (title, alias, slug, |label). work/_index.md lists the profile and projects with note counts."},{"markdown":"Root resolves from `--root`, `OWO_ROOT`, `root` in the nearest `.owo.toml`, `root` in `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/owo/config.toml`, then `$XDG_DATA_HOME/owo`.","startLine":107,"endLine":107,"text":"Root resolves from --root, OWO_ROOT, root in the nearest .owo.toml, root in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/owo/config.toml, then $XDG_DATA_HOME/owo."},{"markdown":"When the root comes from a `.owo.toml` in a parent of the working folder, owo prints a warning on stderr that names that file, since a cloned repo can ship one.","startLine":109,"endLine":109,"text":"When the root comes from a .owo.toml in a parent of the working folder, owo prints a warning on stderr that names that file, since a cloned repo can ship one."},{"markdown":"Identity resolves from `-i`, `OWO_IDENTITY`, `.owo.toml`, user config, then the only identity in the root. Project resolves from `--project`, `OWO_PROJECT`, `.owo.toml`; see [[decisions#Working project versus project filter]]. Relative `root` and `kb` values resolve against the config file's folder; `~/` expands to `$HOME`.","startLine":111,"endLine":111,"text":"Identity resolves from -i, OWO_IDENTITY, .owo.toml, user config, then the only identity in the root. Project resolves from --project, OWO_PROJECT, .owo.toml; see decisions#Working project versus project filter. Relative root and kb values resolve against the config file's folder; ~/ expands to $HOME."},{"markdown":"Templates are embedded in the binary. `<root>/.templates/<name>` overrides one, where `<name>` is the identity-relative path for identity files (`soul/IDENTITY.md`, `work/README.md`) and `<type>.md` for entries (`character.md`).","startLine":115,"endLine":115,"text":"Templates are embedded in the binary. <root>/.templates/<name> overrides one, where <name> is the identity-relative path for identity files (soul/IDENTITY.md, work/README.md) and <type>.md for entries (character.md)."},{"markdown":"Placeholders are `{{name}}`, `{{slug}}`, `{{title}}`, `{{today}}`, `{{date}}`, `{{parent}}`, `{{project}}`. A `{{key_yaml}}` form escapes double quotes for YAML strings, and a `{{key_json}}` form escapes for JSON strings. An era's `start` and `end` are empty until the author sets them.","startLine":117,"endLine":117,"text":"Placeholders are {{name}}, {{slug}}, {{title}}, {{toda